title: CopperDragon Sparrow Framework Binary Executed From Staging Directory
id: 15557d1d-b8ad-4ccb-b30c-48598cfbab7a
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects execution of a binary from one of the staging directories Check
    Point Research attributes to the CopperDragon Sparrow framework used by
    the SilentDelivery, OceanGate and DarkWire clusters. The intrusions park
    implants and droppers under C:\Program Files\7-Zip\Lang (which legitimately
    holds only 7-Zip language files), C:\Windows\debug, C:\ProgramData\Oracle\Java
    and C:\ProgramData\Waves before loading them. A hit means a process was
    launched from a path no legitimate 7-Zip, Oracle Java or Windows debug
    component uses for executables.
references:
    - https://research.checkpoint.com/2026/not-all-that-glitters-is-gold-tracking-copperdragons-sparrow-framework-around-the-globe/
    - https://gbhackers.com/copperdragon-malware-framework/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/11/12
tags:
    - attack.t1036
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_staging_path:
        Image|startswith:
            - 'C:\Program Files\7-Zip\Lang\'
            - 'C:\Windows\debug\'
            - 'C:\ProgramData\Oracle\Java\'
            - 'C:\ProgramData\Waves\'
    filter_lang_files:
        Image|endswith:
            - '.ttt'
            - '.txt'
            - '.log'
    condition: selection_staging_path and not filter_lang_files
falsepositives:
    - Administrators or installers that deliberately drop vendor binaries under C:\Windows\debug or C:\ProgramData\Oracle\Java
    - Software that ships helper executables inside C:\Program Files\7-Zip\Lang (not expected for 7-Zip itself, which stores only language files there)
level: high
